{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1484255-kalindo-like-martial-art-for-kinfolk","id":1484255,"title":"Kalindo-like martial art for Kinfolk","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-16T19:27:21-07:00","id":1484255,"title":"Kalindo-like martial art for Kinfolk","content":"So I saw a topic somewhere about alternative Kalindo &quot;schools&quot; with different spirits. And I begun to think about it. What If Stargazer kinfolk had their own spirit martial art?<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't propose this as somthing as effective as Kalindo. Im actually thinking about a martial art that focus on survival and dodging attacks, something the stargazers come up to make their precious kinfolk harder to kill.<br /> <br /> <br /> I thought about a true harmless martial art, learned and practiced with spirits of peace/serenity. An art that allows kinfolk to dodge/deflect hits with extreme precision as long as they focus only on defending, not attacking. With it the kinfolk movements are so precise and graceful that they can dodge even bullets but inches. But if they try to attack they cannot use it for a scene. This way it makes total sense that stargazers don't learn that and no one will try to combo it with kalindo too. Also, the Stargazers proposely made it so this art cannot be used against their own by a ill intentioned kinfolk.<br /> <br /> <br /> I brainstormed 2 different systems, don't know which makes more sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the first the martial art is a skill, and any simples roll of this skill + dexterity that gets more successes than the attack will allow the kiinfolk to dodge it. It's nor terribly overpower considering that even a ultimate master kinfolk will have at max a 10 dicepool, while many WTA enemies can get beyond that.<br /> <br /> <br /> The other version is a merit. If you have the merit you can add your gnosis pool as extra dice when trying to dodge, and spending one gnosis point allows you to automatically dodge a single attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> In both versions if the kinfolk fight back or do something to hurt anyone, they cannot use the martial art for a scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you think? Oh, and what name could it have?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","user":"Rucun","date":". 06-16-2022, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T19:51:00-07:00","id":1484257,"title":"","content":"I'm not a fan of some larger mechanics around it, but M20 has a Martial Arts trait that lets you pick maneuvers for your character, and you can focus on defensive and non-damaging ones to do this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T14:03:30-07:00","id":1484386,"title":"","content":"I don't think this is so much how any of this works.<br /> <br /> First, Kailindo is a mundane ability as far as it goes. While there is a link to wind spirits, it isn't a magical thing, just a martial art. And it is specially relevant just because of the shapeshifting maneuvers (that aren't exactly supernatural in the sense that the Garou must be capable of this previously on their own). So developing an art for their kinfolk would be nice, but making it outright magical would be weird. Also, most Kinfolk don't have Gnosis (it is exceedingly rare) to begin with, and making an ability impossible to use seems very strange and very heavy-handed, specially a defensive Ability that won't cause a lot of problems anyway.<br /> <br /> Second, any new Martial-Arts style must have a design reason to be. Why not just use the normal Brawl rules? What will make it unique and interesting, yet not simply superior so you may still want the usual? How does it interact with the normal rules? Kailindo's purpose is to bring precise shapeshifting into combat as a part of your combat actions, Do's purpose is to interact with Akashayana's Magic, both give up some common maneuvers to change the repertoire. What will this &quot;Kin-do&quot; bring to the table, and how?<br /> <br /> My take is that you can start from your first idea, but instead of using it as is you should re-read the Defensive Actions section, maybe come up with a list of maneuvers, and take care to not simply make Dodge irrelevant in the process.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, if you really want to make something more magical for the Kinfolk with Gnosis, then it would have to be something that really uses their Gnosis not just for self-defense, but defense of the entire community. And then go wild with Merits, Gifts and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T16:55:49-07:00","id":1484399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1484255-kalindo-like-martial-art-for-kinfolk?p=1484386#post1484386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this is so much how any of this works.<br /> <br /> First, Kailindo is a mundane ability as far as it goes. While there is a link to wind spirits, it isn't a magical thing, just a martial art. And it is specially relevant just because of the shapeshifting maneuvers (that aren't exactly supernatural in the sense that the Garou must be capable of this previously on their own). So developing an art for their kinfolk would be nice, but making it outright magical would be weird. Also, most Kinfolk don't have Gnosis (it is exceedingly rare) to begin with, and making an ability impossible to use seems very strange and very heavy-handed, specially a defensive Ability that won't cause a lot of problems anyway.<br /> <br /> Second, any new Martial-Arts style must have a design reason to be. Why not just use the normal Brawl rules? What will make it unique and interesting, yet not simply superior so you may still want the usual? How does it interact with the normal rules? Kailindo's purpose is to bring precise shapeshifting into combat as a part of your combat actions, Do's purpose is to interact with Akashayana's Magic, both give up some common maneuvers to change the repertoire. What will this &quot;Kin-do&quot; bring to the table, and how?<br /> <br /> My take is that you can start from your first idea, but instead of using it as is you should re-read the Defensive Actions section, maybe come up with a list of maneuvers, and take care to not simply make Dodge irrelevant in the process.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, if you really want to make something more magical for the Kinfolk with Gnosis, then it would have to be something that really uses their Gnosis not just for self-defense, but defense of the entire community. And then go wild with Merits, Gifts and such.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thanks, Im still fiddling with the idea. Top be fair I approached this more interested in cultural aspect, something to enrich the lore of kinfolk and stargazers. I didn't think seriously about real uses for it in combat, or which role to fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T19:47:36-07:00","id":1484410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rucun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1484255-kalindo-like-martial-art-for-kinfolk?p=1484399#post1484399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, Im still fiddling with the idea. Top be fair I approached this more interested in cultural aspect, something to enrich the lore of kinfolk and stargazers. I didn't think seriously about real uses for it in combat, or which role to fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought so, but this is something that regularly brings problems with design, when you make a mechanic or power without mechanical reasons to be.<br /> <br /> Think about the fact that most martial arts are in practice just plain old Brawl, at most specialties in Brawl (however they think we'll be able to apply that fact). You can write an entire book just discussing their particular martial art, its philosophy, their usual training and way of fighting, how it integrates in Stargazer Kinfolk society... and yet be just a Brawl specialty. This neatly covers the cultural aspect without any need for creating a new set of rules just to make them more unique.<br /> <br /> Look at how many players complain about Discipline overload in old Vampire because a lot of redundant and ill-devised powers are created just for the sake of giving &quot;cultural&quot; powers to a bloodline. Some got trimmed down with time by the authors, but it certainly got out of hand.<br /> <br /> Rules need a reason. While it is true that Kailindo and Do both got created just to have Asian Martial Arts in the game, they ended up with a more clear mechanical niche (specially Kailindo, I still have my reservations about Do, and I mostly play as Akashayana). Don't just scrap the idea if you really want it, but you must start to look at it as a designer to have an interesting result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T09:57:05-07:00","id":1484426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1484255-kalindo-like-martial-art-for-kinfolk?p=1484410#post1484410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought so, but this is something that regularly brings problems with design, when you make a mechanic or power without mechanical reasons to be.<br /> <br /> Think about the fact that most martial arts are in practice just plain old Brawl, at most specialties in Brawl (however they think we'll be able to apply that fact). You can write an entire book just discussing their particular martial art, its philosophy, their usual training and way of fighting, how it integrates in Stargazer Kinfolk society... and yet be just a Brawl specialty. This neatly covers the cultural aspect without any need for creating a new set of rules just to make them more unique.<br /> <br /> Look at how many players complain about Discipline overload in old Vampire because a lot of redundant and ill-devised powers are created just for the sake of giving &quot;cultural&quot; powers to a bloodline. Some got trimmed down with time by the authors, but it certainly got out of hand.<br /> <br /> Rules need a reason. While it is true that Kailindo and Do both got created just to have Asian Martial Arts in the game, they ended up with a more clear mechanical niche (specially Kailindo, I still have my reservations about Do, and I mostly play as Akashayana). Don't just scrap the idea if you really want it, but you must start to look at it as a designer to have an interesting result.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fantastic advice! This makes s lot of sense. For me the rules are an after thought and I think sometimes I feel compelled to make up some rule for it just because I feel everything must have a rule even if I don't like making them. Your comment was very insightful on how this can bloat the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}